Under Gunyah, the hypervisor provides the caller's SCM identity for QSEE
trusted-app and trusted-OS SMC64 calls. Booted at EL2 without Gunyah,
x7 is 0 unless qcom,qseecom-client-id provides it.

Set qcom,qseecom-client-id to QCOM_SCM_VMID_HLOS on the hamoa SCM node,
so EL1 and EL2 device trees carry the same value

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/hamoa.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/hamoa.dtsi
@@ -333,6 +333,8 @@
 			interconnects = <&aggre2_noc MASTER_CRYPTO QCOM_ICC_TAG_ALWAYS
 					 &mc_virt SLAVE_EBI1 QCOM_ICC_TAG_ALWAYS>;
 			qcom,dload-mode = <&tcsr 0x19000>;
+			/* QSEE caller (x7); required at EL2, where no hypervisor sets it */
+			qcom,qseecom-client-id = <QCOM_SCM_VMID_HLOS>;
 		};
 
 		scmi {
